WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.520
Pitchers

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.250
Pitching rules are a headache.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:10.780
The app knows who can pitch tonight: their remaining innings, and the required rest.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.520
In Auto mode, it picks the pitchers and their innings according to the Baseball Québec rules.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:24.280
Or set your own rotation: six pitchers at one inning each, or three pitchers at two innings each. Your call.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.500
Tap the pattern, then choose who pitches each block. The others stay on Auto.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.770
And from July first, the limits adjust on their own: one, two, three becomes allowed.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:42.660
After the game, enter the pitch counts: the required rest is calculated for what’s next.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.070
BaseballLineup. Less paperwork, more baseball.
